# .boundary-terms — this repo's disclosure boundary. LOCAL ONLY.
#
# Terms listed here must never cross into committed state: the floor blocks
# any commit whose staged additions, filenames, or message contain one.
# This file is gitignored and must never be committed — the check errors if
# it is ever tracked. The tool ships the capability; the vocabulary is yours.
#
# One term per line. Case-insensitive literal substring match.
# Optionally name the approved substitute after `==>` — the block message
# will suggest it at the moment of violation:
#
#   [client-name] ==> the client
#   [person-name] ==> the second operator
#   [internal-identifier]
